---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Fabio Steyer — Data analytics, automation, applied AI"
  description="Physicist (M.Sc., TU Berlin) with process automation running in production. Projects, evidence, contact."
  altHref="/"
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Fabio Steyer</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-lg" style="color: var(--color-muted)">
    Data analytics · Automation · Applied AI
  </p>

  <p class="mt-8 leading-relaxed">
    Physicist (M.Sc. TU Berlin, thesis phase) with process automation that ran in daily
    operation. I take apart grown workflows, decide per step whether a script or a language
    model fits, and carry the result from prototype into production.
  </p>

  <section class="mt-14" aria-labelledby="projects">
    <h2 id="projects" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Projects</h2>

    <div class="beleg-fehlt mt-4">
      <strong>EVIDENCE MISSING.</strong> This section lists only projects with a publicly
      verifiable artefact — repository, runnable demo, tests. It stays empty until the first
      clean-room repository exists. This notice must be gone before publication.
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4 text-sm" style="color: var(--color-muted)">
      In progress: a small public demonstration project with synthetic data, a reproducible
      setup and tests.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14" aria-labelledby="background">
    <h2 id="background" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Background</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        <strong>Process automation at Cavator Bauausführung (05/2025–05/2026).</strong>{' '}
        A Python pipeline reconciling roughly 3,000 PDF invoices and quotes; a document
        generator; an extraction module for wholesaler price data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bar management at Berndhain.</strong>{' '}Led a team of ten; raised daily revenue
        on strong weekdays by 30 to 40 percent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Physics.</strong>{' '}M.Sc. at TU Berlin, theoretical physics; B.Sc. completed in
        2023 with experimental work on UVC LEDs.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-5 text-sm" style="color: var(--color-muted)">
      The work projects were built inside a company and are therefore not publicly accessible.
      Whatever becomes publicly verifiable will appear under Projects.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
